  <sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Detachment" hidden="false" id="821b-9477-6c47-eab5" defaultSelectionEntryId="none" collapsible="false">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="b9e4-7c28-627a-bac6"/>
        <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="23da-d33f-3805-f52e"/>
      </constraints>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Black Spear Task Force" hidden="false" id="4459-12f0-bc-142b">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="notInstanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="primary-catalogue" childId="f89b-84e0-6e3b-f1e2" shared="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
            <modifier type="set" value="2" field="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="d62d-db22-4893-4bc0" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Kill Teams" id="8472-7f00-395e-e104" hidden="false">
              <description>Each time an attack targets a KILL TEAM unit from your army that contains models with different Toughness characteristics, until the attacking unit has finished making its attacks, use the Toughness characteristic of the majority of the models in that unit when determining what result is required for that attack to successfully wound. If two or more Toughness characteristics are tied for majority, use the highest Toughness characteristic.

For the purposes of determining which models can embark within a TRANSPORT model, KILL TEAM models follow the normal restrictions listed on the TRANSPORT model.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Mission Tactics" id="ab94-6f80-af0b-a719" hidden="false">
              <comment>sim-mod: source=&quot;Mission Tactics (Furor)&quot; sustained=1 conditional choice=&quot;mission-tactics&quot;
sim-mod: source=&quot;Mission Tactics (Malleus)&quot; lethal conditional choice=&quot;mission-tactics&quot;</comment>
              <description>Friendly **^^KILL TEAM^^** units with this ability have the following abilities:

Furor Tactics: If the devastator doctrine is active for your unit, your unit’s attacks have **[SUSTAINED HITS 1]**.
Malleus Tactics: If the tactical doctrine is active for your unit, your unit’s attacks have **[LETHAL HITS]**.
Purgatus Tactics: If the assault doctrine is active for your unit, your unit’s attacks that target an enemy unit within 9&quot; of this unit have &lt;k&gt;[PRECISION]&lt;k&gt;.

RESTRICTIONS: Your army can include **^^ADEPTUS ASTARTES DEATHWATCH^^** units, but it cannot include any **^^ADEPTUS ASTARTES^^** units drawn from any other Chapter.
Your army cannot include any **^^AGENTS OF THE IMPERIUM DEATHWATCH^^** units.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Armour of Contempt (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="234a-1883-a857-0e3a" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=shooting|fight
def-mod: source=&quot;ARMOUR OF CONTEMPT&quot; ap=-1 conditional</comment>
              <description>Black Spear Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Shooting phase or the Fight phase, when an enemy unit targets a friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES unit.
TARGET: That ADEPTUS ASTARTES unit.
EFFECT: Attacks that target your unit have -1 AP until that enemy unit has attacked.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Site-To-Site Teleportation (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="7d1c-6bdf-7e5e-7da6" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=fight</comment>
              <description>Black Spear Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: End of your opponent’s Fight phase.
TARGET: One friendly unengaged ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY unit.
EFFECT: ■ Place your unit in strategic reserves.

■ If your unit has KILL TEAM, your unit has DEEP STRIKE until the end of your next Movement phase.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Adaptive Tactics (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="9a58-cefb-a8dc-fb64" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=command</comment>
              <description>Black Spear Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Command phase.
TARGET: One friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES unit.
EFFECT: Select one combat doctrine. That combat doctrine is active for your unit until the start of your next Command phase.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Hellfire Rounds (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="86df-632b-143b-1077" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=shooting
sim-mod: source=&quot;HELLFIRE ROUNDS&quot; anti=Infantry:2+ anti=Monster:5+ when=ranged kw=&quot;Kill Team&quot;</comment>
              <description>Black Spear Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Shooting phase when a KILL TEAM unit is selected to shoot.
TARGET: That KILL TEAM unit.
EFFECT: Your unit’s ranged attacks (excluding [DEVASTATING WOUNDS] attacks) have [ANTI-&lt;/k&gt;non-&lt;k&gt;VEHICLE 4+].</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Dragonfire Rounds (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="e9ae-3c7c-09cd-8cf2" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=shooting
sim-mod: source=&quot;DRAGONFIRE ROUNDS&quot; ignores-cover when=ranged kw=&quot;Kill Team&quot;</comment>
              <description>Black Spear Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Shooting phase when a KILL TEAM unit is selected to shoot.
TARGET: That KILL TEAM unit.
EFFECT: Your unit’s ranged attacks:
■ Can re-roll wound rolls of 1.
■ Have [IGNORES COVER].</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Kraken Rounds (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="aea0-8eb5-b5ef-4a7f" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=shooting
sim-mod: source=&quot;KRAKEN ROUNDS&quot; ap=+1 when=ranged kw=&quot;Kill Team&quot;</comment>
              <description>Black Spear Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Shooting phase when a KILL TEAM unit is selected to shoot.
TARGET: That KILL TEAM unit.
EFFECT: Your unit’s ranged attacks:
■ Have +6” R.
■ Have +1 S.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="2659-e6fc-6eee-1b42">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Priority Assets</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="c532-8cd5-ccf5-062f">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Purge the Foe</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="DP" typeId="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a" value="3"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Inner Circle Task Force" hidden="false" id="a141-49c8-fd84-4c6d">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="notInstanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="primary-catalogue" childId="470a-6daa-9014-12df" shared="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <costs>
            <cost name="DP" typeId="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a" value="1"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Vowed Target" id="faf6-7377-c475-6b73" hidden="false">
              <comment>sim-mod: source=&quot;Vowed Target&quot; wound=+1 kw=&quot;Deathwing&amp;Infantry&quot; conditional</comment>
              <description>In your Command phase, you can use this ability. If you do, select one objective. That objective is your vowed objective until your next Command phase.
■ Friendly **^^Deathwing Infantry^^** unit’s attacks that target an enemy unit within range of your vowed objective have +1 to wound rolls.

Restrictions: Your army can include **^^Dark Angels^^** units, but it cannot include any **^^Adeptus Astartes^^** units drawn from any other Chapter.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Wrath of the Lion (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="0c46-e8a6-9752-0f74" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=charge</comment>
              <description>Inner Circle Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Charge phase, when a friendly DEATHWING unit ends a charge move.
TARGET: That DEATHWING unit.
EFFECT: Select one enemy unit engaged with your unit. If you do, roll one D6 for each model in your unit engaged with that enemy unit:
■ For each 3+, that enemy unit suffers 1 mortal wound (to a maximum of 6 mortal wounds).</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Duty Unto Death (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="0da2-04cf-d3dc-8a96" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=fight</comment>
              <description>Inner Circle Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Fight phase, when an enemy unit targets a friendly DEATHWING unit.
TARGET: That DEATHWING unit.
EFFECT: When a model in your unit is destroyed, if your unit has not been selected to fight this phase, roll one D6, with +1 to that roll if your unit is engaged with an enemy unit within range of your vowed objective:
■ On a 4+, do not remove that model from the battlefield. When your unit has fought, or at the end of the phase (whichever comes first), that model is removed from the battlefield.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Relic Teleportarium (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="ed9c-10bd-42e0-9b8c" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=movement</comment>
              <description>Inner Circle Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Movement phase, when a friendly DEATHWING unit with the Deep Strike ability is selected to make an ingress move.
TARGET: That DEATHWING unit.
EFFECT: ■ Your unit can be set up more than 6” horizontally from all enemy units (instead of more than 8”).
■ Your unit is not eligible to declare a charge until the end of this turn.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="721e-012b-ec75-72d3">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Priority Assets</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Champions of Fenris" hidden="false" id="afb4-59c7-fa93-55f6">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="notInstanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="primary-catalogue" childId="94bb-3284-ee14-57a1" shared="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <costs>
            <cost name="DP" typeId="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a" value="1"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="The Great Wolf Watches" id="2c17-a29e-62aa-1095" hidden="false">
              <description>Friendly **^^Adeptus Astartes Character^^** units have the following ability:

Countercharge: (Once per battle round, per unit) When you target this unit with the Heroic Intervention stratagem, that use is -1CP.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Champion&apos;s Guidance (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="9098-0554-220a-2af4" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=fight</comment>
              <description>Champions of Fenris – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Fight phase, when a friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES CHARACTER unit is selected to fight.
TARGET: That ADEPTUS ASTARTES CHARACTER unit.
EFFECT: Your unit’s melee attacks can re-roll hit rolls of 1 and wound rolls of 1.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Birth of a Saga (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="92d0-5beb-2193-11fb" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=command</comment>
              <description>Champions of Fenris – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Command phase.
TARGET: One friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES unit (excluding MONSTER/VEHICLE units).
EFFECT: Until the start of your next Command phase, your unit has CHARACTER.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Heroic Resolve (Stratagem, 2CP)" id="6484-cd74-5b94-75a5" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=shooting|fight</comment>
              <description>Champions of Fenris – STRATAGEM (2CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Shooting phase or the Fight phase, when an enemy unit targets a friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES CHARACTER unit.
TARGET: That ADEPTUS ASTARTES CHARACTER unit.
EFFECT: Attacks that target your unit have ‑1 D until that enemy unit has attacked.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="32cf-d3a1-afb8-b752">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Priority Assets</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
