          <costs>
            <cost name="DP" typeId="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a" value="2"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Dutiful Tenacity" id="8c2e-cb8c-57b1-729f" hidden="false">
              <description>Attacks that target friendly **^^Adeptus Astartes Infantry/Mounted^^** units with a S greater than that unit’s T have -1 to wound rolls.

Restrictions: Your army can include **^^Dark Angels^^** units, but it cannot include any **^^Adeptus Astartes^^** units drawn from any other Chapter.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Inescapable Justice (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="32d7-0912-a205-821c" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=fight</comment>
              <description>Wrath of the Rock – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: The Fight phase, when a friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES unit is selected to fight.
TARGET: That ADEPTUS ASTARTES unit.
EFFECT: Your unit&apos;s melee attacks have [Precision].</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Tactical Mastery (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="af82-cc94-6ae7-dda8" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=command</comment>
              <description>Wrath of the Rock – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Command phase.
TARGET: One friendly DEATHWING/RAVENWING unit.
EFFECT: Select one combat doctrine. That combat doctrine is active for your unit until the start of your next Command phase.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Lion&apos;s Will (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="c0dc-1fde-3c7c-f73b" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=command
sim-mod: source=&quot;LION&apos;S WILL&quot; hit=+1 conditional</comment>
              <description>Wrath of the Rock – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Command phase.
TARGET: One friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES unit that is within range of an objective.
EFFECT: Your unit has +1 OC until the end of the turn.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Relics of the Dark Age (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="07b7-da82-3b61-bf77" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=shooting
sim-mod: source=&quot;RELICS OF THE DARK AGE&quot; str=+2 when=ranged kw=&quot;Infantry,Mounted&quot;</comment>
              <description>Wrath of the Rock – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Shooting phase, when a friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY/MOUNTED unit is selected to shoot.
TARGET: That ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY/MOUNTED unit.
EFFECT: Your unit’s ranged attacks have +2 S.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="In Sacrifice, Victory (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="7536-9d7e-a3fa-d279" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=any</comment>
              <description>Wrath of the Rock – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Any phase, when a friendly DEATHWING/RAVENWING unit within range of an objective is destroyed.
TARGET: That DEATHWING/RAVENWING unit. You can target that unit with this stratagem even though it is destroyed.
EFFECT: Select one objective:
■ That no enemy units (excluding AIRCRAFT units) are within range of.
■ That your unit was controlling at the end of the previous phase.That objective is secured.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Knights of Iron (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="6745-de8d-16e1-f42f" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=movement|charge</comment>
              <description>Wrath of the Rock – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Movement/Charge phase, when a friendly RAVENWING unit is selected to move or declares a charge.
TARGET: That RAVENWING unit.
EFFECT: Your unit has MOBILE.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="49b9-07ba-9e5e-bfb0">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Take and Hold</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink id="bfd4-3200-0130-5f9d" name="UNIQUE TERMINATOR" hidden="false" targetId="10e2-7b78-e56f-55de" primary="false"/>
          </categoryLinks>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Saga of the Beastslayer" hidden="false" id="98ed-f58a-3e6e-63a6">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="notInstanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="primary-catalogue" childId="94bb-3284-ee14-57a1" shared="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <costs>
            <cost name="DP" typeId="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a" value="1"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Legendary Slayers" id="9b1b-c1c9-2f94-c66f" hidden="false">
              <comment>sim-mod: source=&quot;Legendary Slayers&quot; lethal vs=Character,Monster,Vehicle conditional</comment>
              <description>Attacks made by friendly **^^Blood Claws/Thunderwolf Cavalry/Wulfen^^** units have **[Lethal Hits: Character/Monster/Vehicle]**.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Unbridled Ferocity (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="7db7-df79-95ee-0a9c" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=fight
sim-mod: source=&quot;Unbridled Ferocity&quot; wound=+1 when=melee kw=&quot;Space Wolves&quot;</comment>
              <description>Saga of the Beastslayer – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Fight phase, when a friendly BLOOD CLAWS/THUNDERWOLF CAVALRY/WULFEN unit is selected to fight.
TARGET: That BLOOD CLAWS/THUNDERWOLF CAVALRY/WULFEN unit.
EFFECT: Your unit’s melee attacks have [LANCE].</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Impetuosity (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="23c4-2a77-c177-b27b" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=shooting</comment>
              <description>Saga of the Beastslayer – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Shooting phase, when an enemy unit that targeted a friendly unengaged BLOOD CLAWS/THUNDERWOLF CAVALRY/WULFEN unit has shot.
TARGET: That BLOOD CLAWS/THUNDERWOLF CAVALRY/WULFEN unit.
EFFECT: Your unit can make a surge move of up to D6”.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Co-ordinated Strike (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="e618-cc6e-1ea6-ccd5" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=fight</comment>
              <description>Saga of the Beastslayer – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: End of your opponent’s Fight phase.
TARGET: One unengaged BLOOD CLAWS/THUNDERWOLF CAVALRY/WULFEN unit that is within 9&quot; of one or more battlefield edges.
EFFECT: Place your unit in strategic reserves.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="7387-a016-aa01-ecf3">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Purge the Foe</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Forgefather&apos;s Seekers" hidden="false" id="e073-8fe8-5b59-48f0">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="notInstanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="primary-catalogue" childId="2261-79a5-19d9-1668" shared="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <costs>
            <cost name="DP" typeId="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a" value="2"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Vulkan&apos;s Quest" id="317f-19b4-6fb6-0761" hidden="false">
              <comment>sim-mod: source=&quot;Vulkan&apos;s Quest&quot; str=+1 when=ranged conditional</comment>
              <description>Ranged weapons equipped by Adeptus Astartes models from your army have the [ASSAULT] ability, and each time an attack made such a weapon targets a unit within 12&quot;, add 1 to the Strength characteristic of that attack.


**Seeker&apos;s Companions**


If your army includes Vulkan He&apos;stan, during your turn, each Infernus Squad unit from your army is eligible to do one of the following
- Start to perform an Action in a turn in which it Advanced

- Shoot in a turn in which it started to perform an Action</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Armour of Contempt (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="bbf7-8b03-1454-5d4f" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=shooting|fight
def-mod: source=&quot;Armour of Contempt&quot; ap=-1 conditional</comment>
              <description>Forgefather’s Seekers – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Shooting phase or the Fight phase, just after an enemy unit has selected its targets.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes unit from your army that was selected as the target of one or more of the attacking unit’s attacks.
EFFECT: Until the attacking unit has finished making its attacks, each time an attack targets your unit, worsen the Armour Penetration characteristic of that attack by 1.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Crucible of Battle (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="6dd3-3a5e-a9e4-2e99" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=shooting|fight
sim-mod: source=&quot;Crucible of Battle&quot; wound=+1 kw=&quot;Infantry&quot; conditional</comment>
              <description>Forgefather’s Seekers – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Shooting phase or the Fight phase.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes Infantry unit from your army that has not been selected to shoot or fight this phase.
EFFECT: Until the end of the phase, each time a model in your unit makes an attack that targets the closest eligible target within 6&quot;, add 1 to the Wound roll.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Wrathful Inferno (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="fb62-4405-f405-c551" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=movement</comment>
              <description>Forgefather’s Seekers – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Movement phase, just after an Adeptus Astartes Infantry unit from your army Falls Back.
TARGET: That unit.
EFFECT: Until the end of the turn, your unit is eligible to shoot in a turn in which it Fell Back.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Immolation Protocols (Stratagem, 2CP)" id="1053-7647-9168-b2cb" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=shooting
sim-mod: source=&quot;Immolation Protocols&quot; dev when=ranged weapon=&quot;Torrent&quot;</comment>
              <description>Forgefather’s Seekers – STRATAGEM (2CP)

WHEN: Your Shooting phase.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes unit from your army that has not been selected to shoot this phase.
EFFECT: Until the end of the phase, Torrent weapons equipped by models in your unit have the [DEVASTATING WOUNDS] ability.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Burning Vengeance (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="38b0-e227-2fa8-4310" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=shooting</comment>
              <description>Forgefather’s Seekers – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Shooting phase, just after an enemy unit has shot.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes Transport unit from your army that was selected as the target of one or more of the attacking unit’s attacks.
EFFECT: One unit embarked within that Transport can disembark as if it were your Movement phase, and can then shoot as if it were your Shooting phase, but must target only that enemy unit when doing so, and can only do so if that enemy unit is an eligible target.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Blazing Earth (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="6021-2ad6-d462-4c6d" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=charge</comment>
              <description>Forgefather’s Seekers – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Start of your opponent’s Charge phase.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes unit from your army equipped with one or more Torrent weapons.
EFFECT: Select one enemy unit (excluding Monsters and Vehicles and units with the Fly keyword) within 12&quot; of and visible to your unit. Until the end of the phase, each time that enemy unit declares a charge, subtract 2 from the Charge roll (this is not cumulative with any other negative modifiers to that Charge roll).</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="d16a-2486-cdac-fdec">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Priority Assets</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Shadowmark Talon" hidden="false" id="dd81-2af4-e7d9-bd07">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="notInstanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="primary-catalogue" childId="6e59-e1ee-47ad-6ce5" shared="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <costs>
            <cost name="DP" typeId="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a" value="2"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Masters of Shadow" id="1869-3566-2284-e685" hidden="false">
              <description>Each time a ranged attack targets an Adeptus Astartes unit from your army, unless the attacking model is within 12&quot;, subtract 1 from the Hit roll and the target has the Benefit of Cover against that attack.


**Unparalled Tactician**

Once per battle round, if an **^^Aethon^^** Shaan model from your army is on the battlefield, you can use the Into Darkness Stratagem for 0CP.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Armour of Contempt (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="9118-9d60-3c36-1a5b" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=shooting|fight
def-mod: source=&quot;Armour of Contempt&quot; ap=-1 conditional</comment>
              <description>Shadowmark Talon – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Shooting phase or the Fight phase, just after an enemy unit has selected its targets.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes unit from your army that was selected as the target of one or more of the attacking unit’s attacks.
EFFECT: Until the attacking unit has finished making its attacks, each time an attack targets your unit, worsen the Armour Penetration characteristic of that attack by 1.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Lay Low the Tyrants (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="95ba-0029-58fd-f849" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=fight</comment>
              <description>Shadowmark Talon – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Fight phase.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes Infantry unit from your army that has not been selected to fight this phase.
EFFECT: Until the end of the phase, melee weapons equipped by models in your unit have the [PRECISION] ability.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Feint and Thrust (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="67d0-cb2a-e867-7eee" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=movement</comment>
              <description>Shadowmark Talon – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Movement phase.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes unit from your army.
EFFECT: Until the end of the turn, your unit is eligible to shoot and declare a charge in a turn in which it Fell Back. If it is a Phobos or Scout Squad unit, it is also eligible to shoot and declare a charge in a turn in which it Advanced.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Stunning Fusillade (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="db09-4fa4-ecd1-a920" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=shooting
sim-mod: source=&quot;Stunning Fusillade&quot; hit=+1 ap=+1 when=ranged kw=&quot;Infantry&quot; conditional</comment>
              <description>Shadowmark Talon – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Shooting phase.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes Infantry unit from your army that has not been selected to shoot this phase.
EFFECT: Until the end of the phase, each time a model in your unit makes a ranged attack that targets an enemy unit that is more than 12&quot; away, improve the Ballistic Skill and Armour Penetration characteristics of that attack by 1. If one or more enemy models are destroyed as a result of those attacks, select one of those destroyed models; that destroyed model’s unit must take a Battle-shock test.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Raptorial Vigilance (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="5207-3327-bf3a-6d90" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=movement</comment>
              <description>Shadowmark Talon – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Movement phase, just after an enemy unit ends a Normal, Advance or Fall Back move.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes Infantry or Adeptus Astartes Mounted unit from your army that is within 9&quot; of the enemy unit that just ended that move. You cannot target a unit that is within Engagement Range of one or more enemy units.
EFFECT: Your unit can make a Normal move of up to D6&quot;, or up to 6&quot; instead if it is a Phobos or Scout Squad unit.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Into Darkness (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="16a1-3b7d-344e-e792" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=fight</comment>
              <description>Shadowmark Talon – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: End of your opponent’s Fight phase.
TARGET: Up to two Phobos and/or Scout Squad units from your army, or one other Adeptus Astartes Infantry unit from your army. You cannot target a unit that is within Engagement Range of one or more enemy units.
EFFECT: Remove those units from the battlefield and place them into Strategic Reserves.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="059a-6a15-8dc2-2a73">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Disruption</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink id="2c09-bedd-762d-1543" name="UNIQUE PHOBOS" hidden="false" targetId="9768-31c6-0185-d488" primary="false"/>
          </categoryLinks>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Spearpoint Task Force" hidden="false" id="0256-e74f-0e54-3e45">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="notInstanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="primary-catalogue" childId="67c1-fc13-f9a1-cbbf" shared="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <costs>
            <cost name="DP" typeId="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a" value="2"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Storm-Swift Onslaught" id="32d2-d63a-d2b0-274a" hidden="false">
              <description>^^**Adeptus Astartes**^^ units from your army are eligible to declare a charge in a turn in which they Advanced or Fell Back.

**Wrath of the First Khan**

At the end of the Fight phase, if a **^^Suboden Khan^^** unit from your army destroyed one or more enemy units this phase and is not within Engagement Range of one or more enemy units, that unit can make a Normal move of up to 6&quot;.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Armour of Contempt (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="ebfc-f815-c46b-e75e" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=shooting|fight
def-mod: source=&quot;Armour of Contempt&quot; ap=-1 conditional</comment>
              <description>Spearpoint Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Shooting phase or the Fight phase, just after an enemy unit has selected its targets.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes unit from your army that was selected as the target of one or more of the attacking unit’s attacks.
EFFECT: Until the attacking unit has finished making its attacks, each time an attack targets your unit, worsen the Armour Penetration characteristic of that attack by 1.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Spear Thrust and Sabre Swing (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="0687-f17d-6bca-8074" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=fight
sim-mod: source=&quot;Spear Thrust and Sabre Swing&quot; wound=+1 when=melee onCharge choice=&quot;spear&quot;
sim-mod: source=&quot;Spear Thrust and Sabre Swing&quot; lethal when=melee choice=&quot;spear&quot;</comment>
              <description>Spearpoint Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Fight phase.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes unit from your army that has not been selected to fight this phase.
EFFECT: Select either the [LANCE] or [LETHAL HITS] ability. Until the end of the phase, melee weapons equipped by models in your unit have the selected ability. If it is a Mounted unit, until the end of the phase, melee weapons equipped by models in your unit have the [LANCE] and [LETHAL HITS] abilities instead.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Mobile Lethality (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="ebdd-32b3-ca9e-69bd" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=movement</comment>
              <description>Spearpoint Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Movement phase.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes unit from your army.
EFFECT: Until the end of the turn, your unit is eligible to shoot in a turn in which it Advanced or Fell Back.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Hunter’s Instincts (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="32f4-6a54-b101-165a" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=movement</comment>
              <description>Spearpoint Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Movement phase, just after an enemy unit ends a Normal, Advance or Fall Back move.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes Infantry unit or Adeptus Astartes Mounted unit from your army that is within 8&quot; of that enemy unit. You cannot target a unit that is within Engagement Range of one or more enemy units.
EFFECT: Your unit can make a Normal move of up to 6&quot;.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Evasive Manoeuvres (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="5a0d-dae7-17cb-b0f9" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=shooting
def-mod: source=&quot;Evasive Manoeuvres&quot; wound=-1 conditional</comment>
              <description>Spearpoint Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Shooting phase, just after an enemy unit has selected its targets.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes Mounted or Adeptus Astartes Fly Vehicle unit from your army that was selected as the target of one or more of the attacking unit’s attacks.
EFFECT: Until the end of the phase, each time an attack targets your unit, subtract 1 from the Wound roll.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Withdraw and Regroup (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="bb50-fb5c-0016-5ed8" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=fight</comment>
              <description>Spearpoint Task Force – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: End of your opponent’s Fight phase.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes Mounted or Adeptus Astartes Fly Vehicle unit from your army that is not within Engagement Range of one or more enemy units.
EFFECT: Remove your unit from the battlefield and place it into Strategic Reserves.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="2244-3728-6245-8f28">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Reconnaissance</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Blade of Ultramar" hidden="false" id="6d9d-6462-1738-6bb3">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="notInstanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="primary-catalogue" childId="4029-9237-e8db-af55" shared="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
            <modifier type="set" value="2" field="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="d62d-db22-4893-4bc0" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <costs>
            <cost name="DP" typeId="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a" value="3"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Mastered Doctrines" id="b260-a005-ff0e-1fbc" hidden="false">
              <description>At the start of up to three of your Command phases, you can select one of the Combat Doctrines listed below. Until the start of your next Command phase, that Combat Doctrine is active and its effects apply to all ^^**Adeptus Astartes^^** units from your army. You cannot select a Combat Doctrine you have already selected this battle, unless a friendly **^^Marneus Calgar^^** model is on the battlefield.

**DEVASTATOR DOCTRINE**
This unit is eligible to shoot in a turn in which it Advanced.

**TACTICAL DOCTRINE**
This unit is eligible to shoot and declare a charge in a turn in which it Fell Back.

**ASSAULT DOCTRINE**
This unit is eligible to declare a charge in a turn in which it Advanced.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Armour of Contempt (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="cf5b-8df4-f641-2199" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=shooting|fight
def-mod: source=&quot;Armour of Contempt&quot; ap=-1 conditional</comment>
              <description>Blade of Ultramar – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Shooting phase or the Fight phase, just after an enemy unit has selected its targets.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes unit from your army that was selected as the target of one or more of the attacking unit’s attacks.
EFFECT: Until the attacking unit has finished making its attacks, each time an attack targets your unit, worsen the Armour Penetration characteristic of that attack by 1.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Tactical Foresight (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="1cf3-b2ea-99ee-1e19" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=shooting|fight
def-mod: source=&quot;Tactical Foresight&quot; wound=-1 vsStronger conditional</comment>
              <description>Blade of Ultramar – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Shooting phase or the Fight phase, just after an enemy unit has selected its targets.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes unit from your army that was selected as the target of one or more of the attacking unit’s attacks.
EFFECT: Until the end of the phase, each time an attack targets your unit, if the Strength characteristic of that attack is greater than or equal to the Toughness characteristic of that unit, subtract 1 from the Wound roll.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Courage and Honour! (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="de7c-ec0d-c03b-073c" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=fight
sim-mod: source=&quot;Courage and Honour!&quot; wound=+1 when=melee onCharge
sim-mod: source=&quot;Courage and Honour!&quot; ap=+1 when=melee conditional</comment>
              <description>Blade of Ultramar – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Fight phase.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes unit from your army.
EFFECT: Until the end of the phase, melee weapons equipped by models in your unit have the [LANCE] ability. If your unit is under the effects of the Assault Doctrine, until the end of the phase, improve the Armour Penetration characteristic of such weapons by 1 as well.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Ultramarian Adaptivity (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="e17c-a924-fbc6-d0d2" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=command</comment>
              <description>Blade of Ultramar – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Command phase.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes unit from your army.
EFFECT: Select the Devastator Doctrine, Tactical Doctrine or Assault Doctrine. Until the start of your next Command phase, that Combat Doctrine is active for your unit instead of any other Combat Doctrine that is active for your army, even if you have already selected that Combat Doctrine this battle.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Exemplary Vigilance (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="b54b-f656-3c5e-b870" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=shooting
sim-mod: source=&quot;Exemplary Vigilance&quot; ignores-cover when=ranged
sim-mod: source=&quot;Exemplary Vigilance&quot; ap=+1 when=ranged conditional</comment>
              <description>Blade of Ultramar – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Shooting phase.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes unit from your army that has not been selected to shoot this phase.
EFFECT: Until the end of the phase, ranged weapons equipped by models in your unit have the [IGNORES COVER] ability. If your unit is under the effects of the Devastator Doctrine, until the end of the phase, improve the Armour Penetration characteristic of such weapons by 1 as well.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Practical Tactics (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="7555-24bb-93ab-b0f6" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=movement</comment>
              <description>Blade of Ultramar – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Movement phase, just after an enemy unit ends a Normal, Advance or Fall Back move.
TARGET: One Adeptus Astartes Infantry or Adeptus Astartes Mounted unit from your army that is not within Engagement Range of one or more enemy units and is within 8&quot; of the enemy unit that just ended that move.
EFFECT: Your unit can make a Normal move of up to D6&quot;, or a Normal move of up to 6&quot; instead if it is under the effects of the Tactical Doctrine.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="7df4-53d1-ae28-0cc7">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Take and Hold</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="4b01-78aa-df67-0b1b">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Priority Assets</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Saga of the Great Wolf" hidden="false" id="bc26-5cb8-f5fb-2760">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="notInstanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="primary-catalogue" childId="94bb-3284-ee14-57a1" shared="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <costs>
            <cost name="DP" typeId="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a" value="2"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Master of Wolves" id="d02f-b1eb-9dcc-fd33" hidden="false">
              <comment>sim-mod: source=&quot;Master of Wolves (Hunter&apos;s Eye)&quot; hit=+1 when=ranged conditional choice=&quot;hunting-pack&quot;
sim-mod: source=&quot;Master of Wolves (Ferocious Strike, Lethal)&quot; lethal when=melee conditional choice=&quot;hunting-pack&quot;
sim-mod: source=&quot;Master of Wolves (Ferocious Strike, Sustained)&quot; sustained=1 when=melee conditional choice=&quot;hunting-pack&quot;</comment>
              <description>Friendly **^^ADEPTUS ASTARTES^^** units (excluding **^^MONSTER/VEHICLES^^** units) with this ability have the following abilities:

Encircling Jaws: If the assault doctrine is active for your unit, your unit has +1 to advance rolls and charge rolls.
Hunter’s Eye: If the devastator doctrine is active for your unit, your unit’s ranged attacks can re-roll hit rolls of 1.
Ferocious Strike: If the tactical doctrine is active for your unit, your unit’s attacks that target an enemy unit with 9” have **[Sustained Hits 1]**.

Friendly **^^Logan Grimnar^^** units have the following ability:

Howling Onslaught: (Once per battle, per army) In your command phase, you can use this ability. If you do, friendly **^^Adeptus Astartes Monster/Vehicle^^** units benefit from the Master of Wolves rule until the start of your next command phase.

Restrictions: Your army can include **^^Space Wolves^^** units, but it cannot include any **^^Adeptus Astartes^^** units drawn from any other Chapter.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Fenrisian Ferocity (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="64b1-5322-f40a-2ec0" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=movement|charge</comment>
              <description>Saga of the Great Wolf – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Movement/Charge phase, when a friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES MOUNTED/WALKER unit is selected to move or declares a charge.
TARGET: That ADEPTUS ASTARTES MOUNTED/WALKER unit.
EFFECT: Your unit has MOBILE.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Grimnar&apos;s Command (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="8b00-8023-21fd-14d1" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=command</comment>
              <description>Saga of the Great Wolf – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Command phase.
TARGET: One friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES unit (excluding MONSTER/VEHICLE units).
EFFECT: Select one combat doctrine. That combat doctrine is active for your unit until the start of your next Command phase.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Battle Instincts (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="30bf-23d5-bac8-637a" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=shooting</comment>
              <description>Saga of the Great Wolf – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Shooting phase, when an enemy unit that targeted a friendly unengaged ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY/MOUNTED unit has shot.
TARGET: That ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY/MOUNTED unit.
EFFECT: Your unit can make a normal move of up to D3+3”.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Eye of the Pack (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="c2b7-c22b-cdc9-9aa0" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=shooting|fight
sim-mod: source=&quot;Eye of the Pack&quot; wound=+1 when=ranged</comment>
              <description>Saga of the Great Wolf – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Shooting phase, or the Fight phase, when a friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY unit is selected to attack.
TARGET: That ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY unit.
EFFECT: Your unit’s attacks can re-roll wound rolls of 1 and 2.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Wolf Totems (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="93a5-ef24-9fab-5b20" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=any
def-mod: source=&quot;Wolf Totems&quot; fnp=5 mortal conditional</comment>
              <description>Saga of the Great Wolf – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Any phase, when a friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY/MOUNTED unit suffers a mortal wound.
TARGET: That ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY/MOUNTED unit.
EFFECT: Your unit has Feel No Pain 5+ against mortal wounds.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Fangs of the Pack (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="fbd5-61a4-b47e-5bfa" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=fight</comment>
              <description>Saga of the Great Wolf – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Fight phase, when a friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY/MOUNTED unit is selected to fight.
TARGET: That ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY/MOUNTED unit.
EFFECT: Your unit’s melee attacks have [Precision].</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="f976-2196-49c3-5aeb">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Take and Hold</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Darkflight Pursuit" hidden="false" id="0f45-c398-9737-cf9a">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="notInstanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="primary-catalogue" childId="470a-6daa-9014-12df" shared="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <costs>
            <cost name="DP" typeId="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a" value="1"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Black-winged Vigilance" id="968c-1f9f-1520-6159" hidden="false">
              <comment>sim-mod: source=&quot;Black-winged Vigilance&quot; ignores-cover when=ranged conditional</comment>
              <description>Friendly **^^Ravenwing Fly^^** units&apos; ranged attacks have **[IGNORES COVER]**.

Restrictions: Your army can include **^^Dark Angels^^** units, but it cannot include any **^^Adeptus Astartes^^** units drawn from any other Chapter.

Friendly **^^Outrider squad^^** units have **^^Battleline^^**.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Skyborne Surveillance (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="acb7-f3da-2700-2447" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=shooting</comment>
              <description>Darkflight Pursuit – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Shooting phase, when a friendly RAVENWING FLY unit has shot.
TARGET: That RAVENWING FLY unit.
EFFECT: Visible enemy units within 6&quot; of your unit have +3&quot; detection range.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Wings of Shadow (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="afc2-651f-f02b-7cd4" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=shooting</comment>
              <description>Darkflight Pursuit – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent&apos;s Shooting phase, when an enemy unit targets a friendly RAVENWING FLY/MOUNTED unit.
TARGET: That RAVENWING FLY/MOUNTED unit.
EFFECT: Your unit has Stealth.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="We Are Vengeance (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="6725-348a-0562-d273" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=shooting</comment>
              <description>Darkflight Pursuit – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent's Shooting phase, when an enemy unit that targeted a friendly unengaged RAVENWING FLY unit has shot.
TARGET: That RAVENWING FLY unit.
EFFECT: Your unit can make a normal move of up to D3+3&quot;.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="e791-786f-5942-f282">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Reconnaissance</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Marshal's Household" hidden="false" id="29cd-4f6f-487d-0034">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="notInstanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="primary-catalogue" childId="36d3-36bc-68dd-40ac" shared="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <costs>
            <cost name="DP" typeId="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a" value="1"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Faith-fuelled Resolve" id="bdda-e7bc-7e11-a653" hidden="false">
              <comment>sim-mod: source=&quot;Faith-fuelled Resolve&quot; attacks=+1 when=melee kw=&quot;Sword Brethren Squad&quot; conditional</comment>
              <description>In the Fight phase, if a friendly **^^Sword Brethren Squad^^** unit is within range of an objective, that unit’s melee attacks have +1 A.

**Restrictions:** Your army can include **^^Black Templars^^** units, but it cannot include any **^^Adeptus Astartes^^** units drawn from any other Chapter.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Slayers of Abominations (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="7242-bece-24a9-3526" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=fight
sim-mod: source=&quot;Slayers of Abominations&quot; str=+2 when=melee kw=&quot;Sword Brethren Squad&quot; vs=Monster,Vehicle</comment>
              <description>Marshal's Household – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Fight phase, when a friendly SWORD BRETHREN SQUAD unit is selected to fight.
TARGET: That SWORD BRETHREN SQUAD unit.
EFFECT: Your unit's melee attacks that target a MONSTER/VEHICLE unit have +2 S.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Blade of Detestation (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="b20f-7e3c-1ccd-93f1" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=charge</comment>
              <description>Marshal's Household – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Charge phase, when a friendly SWORD BRETHREN SQUAD unit ends a charge move.
TARGET: That SWORD BRETHREN SQUAD unit.
EFFECT: Select one enemy unit engaged with your unit. Roll one D6 for each model in your unit engaged with that enemy unit:
- For each 4+, that enemy unit suffers 1 mortal wound (to a maximum of 6 mortal wounds).</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Unsparing Execution (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="db00-65b9-a7bb-794a" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=movement</comment>
              <description>Marshal's Household – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent's Movement phase, when a unit is selected to make a fall-back move, if that unit is engaged with a friendly SWORD BRETHREN SQUAD unit.
TARGET: That SWORD BRETHREN SQUAD unit.
EFFECT: When an enemy unit engaged with your unit is selected to make a fall-back move, that enemy unit must use the desperate escape mode, with -1 to those hazard rolls if that enemy unit is battle-shocked.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="cf37-aa64-7f4d-2ace">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Priority Assets</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Fist of the God-Emperor" hidden="false" id="2c76-3c2f-6abc-471b">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="notInstanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="primary-catalogue" childId="36d3-36bc-68dd-40ac" shared="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <costs>
            <cost name="DP" typeId="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a" value="1"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Purge and Sanctify" id="b63f-9548-4d44-f1e2" hidden="false">
              <description>Each time a friendly **^^Crusader Squad^^** unit makes a surge move, instead of selecting a surge target, you can select the closest objective to that unit. When that unit makes that surge move, each model in that unit must end that surge move as close as possible to that objective instead.

**Restrictions:** Your army can include **^^Black Templars^^** units, but it cannot include any **^^Adeptus Astartes^^** units drawn from any other Chapter.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Doctrinal Flexibility (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="f736-6a03-f533-d398" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=command</comment>
              <description>Fist of the God-Emperor – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Command phase.
TARGET: One friendly CRUSADER SQUAD unit.
EFFECT: Select one combat doctrine. That combat doctrine is active for your unit until the start of your next Command phase.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Angels Defiant (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="662c-06b4-db69-c608" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=shooting|fight
def-mod: source=&quot;Angels Defiant&quot; wound=-1 vsStronger conditional</comment>
              <description>Fist of the God-Emperor – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Shooting phase or the Fight phase, when an enemy unit targets a friendly CRUSADER SQUAD unit.
TARGET: That CRUSADER SQUAD unit.
EFFECT: Attacks that target your unit with a S greater than your unit’s T have -1 to wound rolls.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Avowed Destruction (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="60e9-7991-7dd0-38b7" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=fight
sim-mod: source=&quot;Avowed Destruction&quot; lethal when=melee conditional choice=&quot;Avowed Destruction&quot;
sim-mod: source=&quot;Avowed Destruction&quot; sustained=1 when=melee conditional choice=&quot;Avowed Destruction&quot;</comment>
              <description>Fist of the God-Emperor – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: The Fight phase, when a friendly CRUSADER SQUAD unit is selected to fight.
TARGET: That CRUSADER SQUAD unit.
EFFECT: Your unit’s melee attacks:
■ Have [LETHAL HITS].
■ Or: Have [SUSTAINED HITS 1].</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="8d77-4a20-69d2-e366">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Take and Hold</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Vow-sworn Crusaders" hidden="false" id="970b-67c8-54db-f4e1">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="notInstanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="primary-catalogue" childId="36d3-36bc-68dd-40ac" shared="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <costs>
            <cost name="DP" typeId="0d99-4ee2-7b3c-1f5a" value="2"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Templar Vows" id="9212-3991-8940-b27e" hidden="false">
              <comment>sim-mod: source=&quot;Templar Vows (Abhor the Witch)&quot; wound=+1 when=melee onCharge vs=Psyker choice=&quot;Templar Vows&quot;
sim-mod: source=&quot;Templar Vows (Accept Any Challenge)&quot; wound=+1 when=melee vsTougher conditional choice=&quot;Templar Vows&quot;</comment>
              <description>At the start of the first battle round, you can select one Vow listed below. That Vow is active for friendly **^^Adeptus Astartes^^** units until the end of the battle.

**Abhor the Witch, Destroy the Witch**
This unit’s melee attacks that target a **^^Psyker^^** unit:
■ Have **[PRECISION]**.
■ Have **[LANCE]**.

**Accept Any Challenge, No Matter the Odds**
Friendly melee attacks that target a unit with a T greater than this unit’s S have +1 to wound rolls.

**Uphold the Honour of the Emperor**
Friendly **^^Infantry^^** units have:
■ At the end of your Movement phase, if this unit is controlling an objective, that objective is secured.
■ When this unit is selected to make an advance move, that advance move does not prevent this unit from being eligible to start an action.

**Restrictions:** Your army can include **^^Black Templars^^** units, but it cannot include any **^^Adeptus Astartes^^** units drawn from any other Chapter.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Dread Crusaders (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="97ee-7e65-a719-fd38" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=charge</comment>
              <description>Vow-sworn Crusaders – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Charge phase, when an enemy unit selects charge targets.
TARGET: One ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY unit that was selected as a charge target by that enemy unit this phase.
EFFECT: That enemy unit must make a battle-shock roll, with -1 to that battle-shock roll.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="For the Emperor&apos;s Honour! (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="04b2-2110-183f-735d" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=fight</comment>
              <description>Vow-sworn Crusaders – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: The Fight phase, when a friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY unit is selected to fight.
TARGET: That ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY unit.
EFFECT: Your unit’s melee attacks have [PRECISION].</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Heresy Begets Retribution (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="31db-b3a9-964e-3859" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=opponent phase=movement</comment>
              <description>Vow-sworn Crusaders – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your opponent’s Movement phase, when an enemy unit ends a move within 8&quot; of a friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY unit.
TARGET: That ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY unit.
EFFECT: Your unit can make a surge move of up to D6&quot;.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Spoor of the Unholy (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="d4d9-ae2f-8323-2478" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=your phase=shooting|fight</comment>
              <description>Vow-sworn Crusaders – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Your Shooting phase or the Fight phase, when a friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES unit is selected to attack.
TARGET: That ADEPTUS ASTARTES unit.
EFFECT: Your unit can ignore modifiers to your unit’s:
■ BS and WS.
■ Hit rolls.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Pious Enmity (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="56d7-9f4f-5deb-c0ca" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=fight
sim-mod: source=&quot;Pious Enmity&quot; reroll=hit1 when=melee conditional choice=&quot;Pious Enmity&quot;
sim-mod: source=&quot;Pious Enmity (Monster/Vehicle)&quot; reroll=hit1 reroll=wound1 when=melee vs=Monster,Vehicle conditional choice=&quot;Pious Enmity&quot;</comment>
              <description>Vow-sworn Crusaders – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Fight phase, when a friendly CHAPLAIN/JUDICIAR unit is selected to fight.
TARGET: That CHAPLAIN/JUDICIAR unit.
EFFECT: ■ Your unit’s melee attacks can re-roll hit rolls of 1.
■ Or: Your unit’s melee attacks that target a MONSTER/VEHICLE unit can re-roll hit rolls of 1 and wound rolls of 1.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Devout Push (Stratagem, 1CP)" id="8543-baf8-5ca8-7935" hidden="false">
              <comment>strat-timing: turn=either phase=fight</comment>
              <description>Vow-sworn Crusaders – STRATAGEM (1CP)

WHEN: Fight phase, when a friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY unit is selected to make a pile-in/consolidation move.
TARGET: That ADEPTUS ASTARTES INFANTRY unit.
EFFECT: When making that pile-in/consolidation move, your unit can move up to D3+3&quot;.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Force Disposition" typeId="4680-63ad-ad70-1872" typeName="Force Disposition" hidden="false" id="eb6d-ab05-befc-9e48">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Force Disposition" typeId="9145-6e6a-17b9-0a2c">Purge the Foe</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
