  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Combat Doctrines" id="3b76-4053-ece9-6e7d" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of your Command phase, you can select one combat doctrine listed below. If you do, that combat doctrine is active for friendly **^^Adeptus Astartes^^** units with this ability until the start of your next Command phase.

ASSAULT DOCTRINE
When this unit is selected to make an advance move, that advance move does not prevent this unit from being eligible to declare a charge.

DEVASTATOR DOCTRINE
This unit’s ranged attacks have **[ASSAULT]**.

TACTICAL DOCTRINE
When this unit is selected to make a fall-back move, that fall-back move does not prevent this unit from being eligible to shoot and eligible to declare a charge.

Unless otherwise stated:
■ You can only select each combat doctrine once per battle.
■ Only one combat doctrine can be active for each unit. If a rule makes a combat doctrine active for a unit, any combat doctrine previously active for that unit is no longer active for that unit.</description>
      <modifiers>
        <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
          <conditions>
            <condition type="instanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="primary-catalogue" childId="36d3-36bc-68dd-40ac" shared="true"/>
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Transhuman Strategist" id="dc23-ec41-a57a-944b" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of the battle round, if a model with this ability is your **^^Warlord^^**, gain 1CP.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Librarius" id="c785-7fe3-ce79-1599" hidden="false">
      <description>**^^Adeptus Astartes Psyker^^** units with this ability have a psyker level of 1 or higher, specified in that unit’s abilities. Each psychic ability has a psychic level of 1 or higher, specified in that ability’s name.

In a battle round, a friendly **^^Adeptus Astartes Psyker^^** unit can use a number of psychic abilities whose total psychic level does not exceed that **^^Psyker^^** unit’s psyker level.

Example: In a battle round, a psyker level 3 **^^Psyker^^** unit could use three psychic level 1 abilities, or one psychic level 1 ability and one psychic level 2 ability, or one psychic level 3 ability.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
  <infoLinks>
    <infoLink name="Combat Doctrines" id="001d-723a-56e2-f202" hidden="false" type="rule" targetId="3b76-4053-ece9-6e7d"/>
  </infoLinks>
</catalogue>
